According to AMD’s Form 10-Q for the quarter ended September 24, 2022 (Accession 0000002488-22-000170), net revenue rose 29% year-over-year.  The increase was driven by:  
• A 45% increase in Data Center revenue, primarily due to higher sales of EPYC™ server processors;  
• A 14% increase in Gaming revenue, primarily due to higher semi-custom product sales;  
• A “significant” increase in Embedded revenue, driven by the inclusion of Xilinx embedded product sales;  
partially offset by a 40% decrease in Client revenue, primarily due to lower processor shipments amid a weak PC market and inventory corrections. (0000002488-22-000170)
